SWEET vsync timer idles when nothing needs it (patch 0190, X-G7, own code; rebased onto 0149 sweet_fb_rearm and 0148 by T-2b87). The 60 Hz AppleCLCD vsync timer (0046, 0056, 0101) re-armed unconditionally, also with no IOMobileFramebufferUserClient registered, so it kept waking 60 times a second while no client is open (read from source; wakeup cost unmeasured). Now vsyncFired re-arms only while AppleCLCD::needsVsync(): a registered client (vsync notifications), a frame waiting (fDirty && !fPowerOff), a blank pass still to do (fPowerOff && fFadeStep == 0) or the QR log holding the panel (sweet_qr_hold); otherwise it parks (fVsyncIdle, fLock) and logs `SWEET FB: vsync timer idle (...)` once. addClient restarts a parked timer and logs `SWEET FB: vsync timer resumed (client)`. fDirty and fPowerOff are only ever set from a client call (swap, selector 72 power path), so a client always exists, hence a running timer, whenever they change. Behaviour with a client is unchanged. Host test tools/test_0190_vsync_idle.py (patch text + mutants). Not run on hardware.

